hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1124","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah! Should we perform ablution after eating goat meat? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, then perform ablution, and if you wish, then do not perform ablution. The man asked: Should we perform ablution after eating camel meat? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He asked: May I pray"
"1125","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah instructed us: Perform ablution after eating camel meat, and do not perform ablution after eating goat meat."""""
"1126","narrated ahadith. Whoever does not have expertise in the science of hadith falls into the misunderstanding that these are two unknown persons. Therefore, you should acquire this understanding—may Allah have mercy on you—so that you do not fall into any misunderstanding regarding this."",""On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ  it is narrated that he was asked about praying in the sleeping places of sheep"",""so he permitted it. He was asked about praying in the sleeping places of camels"","" so he forbade it. And he was asked about making ablution with the meat of sheep"","" so he said"","" """"If you like"","" make ablution with it"","" and if you prefer"","" then do not."""""""""
"1127","""The Messenger of Allah commanded us to perform ablution after eating camel meat but not to perform ablution after eating the mutton."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 495)"
"1128","I understand that what is meant is the ablution which is done for obligatory prayer. It does not mean washing both hands. The reason is, if it meant washing both hands, then the ruling regarding camel meat and goat meat would have been the same. Previously, the ruling was that ablution would be nullified by eating something cooked on fire. This ruling was abrogated, and the ruling regarding camel meat remained as an exception. This exception was made from those things which were later declared permissible, as we have mentioned earlier."
"1129","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) passed by a pot, and he ate from it a piece of meat with bone, then he performed prayer and did not renew his ablution. Imam Abu Hatim (may Allah have mercy on him) states: The statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that ""he ate it"" refers to the meat attached to the bone. Eating the bone itself is not meant. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that then he ate it, refers to the meat that was attached to the bones. Eating the bone itself is not meant."
"1130","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: Bread and meat were presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he ate it. Then he asked for water for ablution and performed the Zuhr prayer. Then he asked for the remaining food and ate it, then performed the Asr prayer and did not perform ablution again. I, along with Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), presented myself before him, and he asked: \""Is there anything (to eat)?\"" but nothing w"
"1131","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) ate the meat of the animal's shoulder (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) or ate the meat of the ribs, then he performed prayer and did not perform ablution again."
"1132","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat, and with him were Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayy"
"1133","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took (the meat of) a (goat's) shoulder and offered prayer and did not perform ablution. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 187)"
"1134","It was reported that Jabir (ra) said ""That last of the two matters from the Messenger ofAllah ﷺ was leaving off ablution from that which had been touched by fire."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 185)"
"1135","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) eat food cooked on fire. He performed the prayer before renewing his ablution. After the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), I saw Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) eat something cooked on fire, then perform the prayer before renewing his ablution. Then after Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), I saw Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) eat someth"
"1136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ate meat. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pl"
"1137","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions ate it. When the time for prayer came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution (and offered the prayer). Then he went towards the remaining portion of the meat and those people ate it. When the time for Asr prayer came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform ablution again."
"1138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the house of an Ansari woman. The narrator states: This woman spread a dining mat for you near the shade of a cluster of date palms and sprinkled water around it. She had slaughtered a goat, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ate its meat. We also ate along with you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took a nap under the cluster of date palms. When he woke up, he performed ablution and offered the Zuhr prayer. The woman submitted: O Messenger of Allah! We have some food left; would you like to eat some more of it? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes. So you ate it. We also ate along with you. Then you offered prayer without performing ablution again."
"1139","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: An Ansari woman invited us. She had slaughtered a goat and prepared food. She had sprinkled water under a cluster of date palms. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for water for ablution, performed ablution, and offered prayer. Then we came to the remaining food, and he ate from it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) offered prayer again and did not perform ablution anew. (Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates:) Once I presented myself to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). He asked for food, but nothing was found to eat. He inquired: Where is that goat of yours which has given birth? His wife replied: It is here. Then he called for it and milked it with his own hand. Then he prepared its laba (a specific type of food). Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) ate it, then he offered prayer and did not perform ablution anew. (Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates:) Once I ate dinner with Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Two bowls were presented before him. One bowl was placed before Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and the other before those present. (All ate the food.) Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) offered prayer and did not perform ablution anew. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Here, the word ""as-suwar"" used in the text of the narration refers to a cluster of date palm trees."
"1140","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took (the meat of) a (goat's) shoulder and offered prayer and did not perform ablution. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 187)"
"1141","I saw Messenger of Allah ﷺ cutting part of the shoulder of mutton with a knife. He ate of it and then was called for prayer whereupon he got up and put down the knife and offered the prayer without performing new ablution. (Using translation from Bukhārī 5422)"
"1142","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ate the meat of a goat’s shoulder and then got up to perform prayer. He performed the prayer without renewing his ablution and without rinsing his mouth."
"1143","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ate the meat of a goat's shoulder, then he performed prayer and did not perform ablution again."
"1144","Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a piece of cooked mutton from the shoulder region and prayed without repeating ablution. (Using translation from Bukhārī 207)"
"1145","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the house of an Ansari woman. She spread a bedding for you near a cluster of date-palm trees. She sprinkled water around it. She slaughtered a goat and prepared food for you. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ate it, and we also ate with you. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution for the Zuhr prayer and then offered the prayer. The woman said: O Messenger of Allah! Some food from the meat of this goat is left with us; would you like to eat it? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ate it, and we also ate it. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the Asr prayer, and he did not perform ablution again."
"1146","I performed ablution? I have eaten pieces of cheese. I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Perform ablution after eating things cooked on fire.'"" Umar bin Abdul Aziz used to perform ablution after eating sugar."
"1147","The narrator's name is Abdullah bin Ibrahim bin Qariz, although his name is Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qariz."
"1148","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Perform ablution after eating something cooked on fire."
"1149","narrates: A goat was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), its stomach was roasted for him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate it. Then he got up and performed prayer, and he did not perform ablution again."
"1150","The narrator named Ishaq has transmitted this narration with his chain from Fadl bin Amr from his father. He did not mention the name of Sayyiduna Amr bin Umayyah al-Damri (may Allah be pleased with him) and he mentioned these words: ""You were eating meat from the bone, then the call for prayer came."" This narrator also transmitted these words: ""You put (the knife) from your hand aside, and performed the prayer, and did not perform ablution again."
"1151","narrates: He saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) perform ablution after eating pieces of cheese. Then he saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) eat the meat of a goat's shoulder and perform prayer without renewing his ablution."
"1152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for food, and only sattu (roasted barley flour) was available. The narrator says: We ate it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) then asked for water, rinsed his mouth, and performed the prayer. He did not perform ablution (wudu) again."
"1153","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) eat goat meat, then he performed prayer. He did not rinse his mouth nor did he touch water (i.e., he did not perform ablution again)."
"1154","A man asked the Messenger of Allah (may peace he upon him) whether he should perform ablution after (eating) mutton. He (the Messenger of Allah) said: Perform ablution it you so desire, and if you do not wish, do not perform it. He (again) asked: Should I perform ablution (after eating) camel's flesh? He said: Yes, perform ablution (after eating) camel's flesh. He (again) said: May I say prayer in the sheepfolds? He (the Messenger of Allah) said: Yes. He (the narrator) again said: May I say prayer where camels lie down? He (the Holy Prophet) said: No. (Using translation from Muslim 360a)"
"1155","The narrator says: When we reached the place of Sahba, which is a location near Khaybar, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) camped there and performed the Asr prayer. Then he ordered food to be brought, but only sattu (barley flour) was presented. By the order of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), it was mixed with water, and then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ate it. We also ate with him. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up to perform the Maghrib prayer, so he rinsed his mouth, and we also rinsed our mouths. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not perform ablution again."
"1156","A man asked the Messenger of Allah (may peace he upon him) whether he should perform ablution after (eating) mutton. He (the Messenger of Allah) said: Perform ablution it you so desire, and if you do not wish, do not perform it. He (again) asked: Should I perform ablution (after eating) camel's flesh? He said: Yes, perform ablution (after eating) camel's flesh. He (again) said: May I say prayer in the sheepfolds? He (the Messenger of Allah) said: Yes. He (the narrator) again said: May I say prayer where camels lie down? He (the Holy Prophet) said: No. (Using translation from Muslim 360a)"
"1157","narrates: It was asked from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about performing ablution after eating goat meat, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If you wish, then perform ablution. He was asked about performing prayer in sheep enclosures, so he said: If you wish, then perform prayer there. He was asked about performing ablution after eating camel meat, so he said: You should perform ablution. He was asked about performing prayer in camel enclosures, so he said: Do not perform prayer at that place."
"1158","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) drank milk, then he asked for a vessel and rinsed his mouth. He said: There is greasiness in it (milk)."
"1159","it contains greasiness. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 196)"
"1160","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by us. We requested: Please come forward. He came forward and ate dates with us, and he did not touch water (i.e., he did not perform ablution again)."
"1161","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who washes the dead should take a bath, and he who carries him should perform ablution. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3161)"
"1162","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a shoulder (of goat's meat) and after wiping his hand with a cloth on which he was sitting, he got up and prayed. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 189)"
"1163","“Step aside and I will show you how.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ put his hand between the skin and the flesh, and thrust his arm in until it disappeared up to the armpit, and said: “O boy, this is how you skin it.” Then he went and led the people in prayer and did not perform Wudu’. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3179)"
"1164","""If water is released then let her perform Ghusl."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 195)"
"1165","The wife of Abu Talhah, Umm Sulaim, came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). She said: O Messenger of Allah! Indeed, Allah does not shy away from the truth. If a woman experiences a wet dream, is ghusl (ritual bath) obligatory upon her? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Yes, if she sees water (i.e., semen), (meaning when her semen has been discharged)."
"1166","I turned towards that woman and said: Woe to you! Does any woman also see such a dream? The noble wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him) narrates: Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned towards this noble wife. He said: May your hands be dusted, then (the resemblance of the child) is because of this."
"1167","(the mother of the believers) Um Sulaim, the wife of Abu Talha, came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Verily Allah is not shy of (telling you) the truth. Is it necessary for a woman to take a bath after she has a wet dream (nocturnal sexual discharge)?"" Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, ""Yes, if she notices a discharge."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 282)"
"1168","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Water (i.e., ghusl) becomes obligatory because of the emission of water (i.e., semen)."
"1169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The woman should wash the moisture that has touched her and perform ablution, then offer prayer."
"1170","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Sayyiduna Ubay"
"1171","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: One day we were walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed by the house of an Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is so-and-so? The narrator says, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for him, and that person quickly came out from inside, with water dripping from his head. The Prophet (peace and bl"
"1172","Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) about a person who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. Sayyiduna Uthman (m"
"1173","""Water is for water,' was only permitted in the beginning of Islam. Then it was prohibited."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 110)"
"1174","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When a man sits between the four parts of a woman and then has intercourse with her, ghusl (ritual bath) becomes obligatory upon him."
"1175","I used to do so, but we both would perform ghusl (ritual bath) in that case."
"1176","I and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) did this, we would perform ghusl."
"1177","the Prophet said: ""When the circumcised meets the circumcised then Ghusl is required."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 109)"
"1178","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a man sits between the four parts of a woman and exerts himself upon her (i.e., has intercourse with her), then ghusl becomes obligatory."" In the narration of the narrator named Matar, these words are present: ""Even if he does not ejaculate."
"1179","The verdict that water (bath) is necessary when there is emission given by the people (in the early days of Islam) was due to the concession granted by the Messenger of Allah in the beginning of Islam. He then commanded to take a bath (in such a case). Abu Dawud said : By Abu Ghassan is meant Muhammad b. mutarrif. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 215)"
"1180","The narrator named Husain is Husain bin Uthman bin Bishr bin Muhtafiz. He was from Basra. He had settled in Marw. He is among the trustworthy narrators."
"1181","I and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) also used to do this, and in such a case, we would perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"1182","""When (a man) sits between the four parts of his wife's body and exerts himself, then Ghusl becomes obligatory."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 191)"
"1183","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'When the two circumcised parts meet, and (the tip of the penis) disappears, then bath is obligatory.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 611)"
"1184","the Prophet said: ""When the circumcised meets the circumcised then Ghusl is required."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 109)"
"1185","I and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) also used to do this, and in such a case, both of us would perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"1186","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). She was asked about a person who engages in intercourse, but his semen does not ejaculate. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied that she and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) also used to do so, and in that case, both of them would perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"1187","I wanted to ask and I had a strong desire that I find someone who could tell me whether the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed the Duha prayer, but I did not find anyone who could inform me about this except Lady Umm Hani bint Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with her). She informed me that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, after the day had advanced, she came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). By the order of the Prophet (peace be upon him), a curtain was put up for him. He performed ghusl (ritual bath), then he stood up and performed eight rak‘ahs. I could not determine whether his standing in these rak‘ahs was longer, or his bowing was longer, or his prostration was longer, or whether all of these were about the same length. Lady Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) states: I did not see the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performing these voluntary prayers before or after this."
"1188","I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the conquest (of Mecca) and found him take a bath. while his daughter Fatimah was holding a curtain around him. (Using translation from Muslim 336a)"
"1189","I came to him, and Abu Dharr al-Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) brought a large vessel of water to the Prophet (peace be upon him). Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I saw traces of flour in that vessel. Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Then Abu Dharr al-Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) set up a curtain for the Prophet (peace be upon him), then he performed ghusl (ritual bath). Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) set up a curtain for Abu Dharr al-Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him), then he performed ghusl. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed eight rak‘ahs of prayer. This was at the time of Duha (forenoon). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) It is possible that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, when the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ghusl, both his daughter Sayyida Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) and Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) set up the curtain for him, using the same cloth. So, the slave of Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her), Abu Murrah, narrated the report in which only Sayyida Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) is mentioned, and Matlub bin Hantab narrated the report in which only Abu Dharr al-Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) is mentioned. In this case, there is no contradiction or difference between the two reports, because on that day the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ghusl only once. That is why, when Abu Dharr al-Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to perform ghusl, the Prophet (peace be upon him) set up the curtain for him. Sayyida Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) did not do so."
"1190","""My maternal aunt Maimunah told me: 'I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water for his Ghusl from Janabah, and he washed his hands two or three times, then he put his right hand in the vessel and poured water over his private part, then he washed it with his left hand. Then he put his left hand on the ground and rubbed it hard. Then he performed Wudu' as for prayer,then poured three scoops with his two hands full of water over his head, then he washed his entire body, then he moved away from where he had been standing and washed his feet.' She said: 'Then I brought him a towel but he refused it.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 253)"
"1191","""Aishah described how the Prophet ﷺ performed Ghusl for Janabah. She said: 'He used to wash his hands three times, then pour water with his right hand onto his left and wash his private part and whatever was on it.' - (One of the narrators) 'Umar said: ""I think he said: 'He would pour water with his right hand onto his left hand three times.'"" - ""Then he would rinse his mouth three times and his nose three times, and wash his face and hands three times, then he would pour water over his head three times, then pour water over himself.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 246)"
"1192","Sayyidah ‘Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): Can a woman perform ghusl of janabah with her husband from the same vessel, while both of them bathe together? Sayyidah ‘Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: Yes, water is pure; janabah does not affect it. I and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform ghusl from the same vessel. I would pour water over your (the Prophet’s) hand before you put your hand into the water."
"1193","""The Messenger of Allah and I would take a bath from a single vessel."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 376)"
"1194","I used to perform ghusl (ritual bath) for janabah from the same vessel. We both used to take water from it with our hands."
"1195","I and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform ghusl from one vessel. While beginning, he would say: Leave some for me, leave some (water) for me as well."
"1196","It was narrated from 'Aishah that when the Prophet ﷺ performed Ghusl from Janabah he would start by washing his hands, then he would perform Wudu' as for prayer, then he would dip his fingers in the water, then run them through his hair, then he would pour water over his head three times, then he would pour water over his entire body. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 247)"
"1197","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform ghusl in a halab. (This refers to the vessel in which the milk of a she-camel is collected.) Its size was such that Abu Asim indicated it with both his hands. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would pour water on his right side, then he would take water in both hands and pour it over his body."
"1198","""I said, O Messenger of Allah! I am a woman with tight braids. Should I undo them when I take a bath to cleanse myself from the state of sexual impurity?"" He said: ""Rather it is sufficient for you to pour three handfuls of water over yourself, and you will be purified,"" or he said: ""In that case you would have become purified."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 603)"
"1199","I purify myself with it? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Purify yourself with it. She again asked: How should I purify myself with it? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his blessed hand on his face and said: Subhan Allah! Purify yourself with it. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I pulled that woman towards myself and explained to her that you should clean the traces of blood with it."
"1200","I purify myself with it? The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: Purify yourself with it. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I understood what the Prophet (peace be upon him) meant, so I pulled the woman towards me and explained the method to her."
"1201","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform ghusl (ritual bath) with a vessel which was called ""Faraq"". He used to perform ghusl for janabah (major ritual impurity)."
"1202","Hafsa, daughter of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abu Bakr, reported that 'A'isha narrated to her that she and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a bath from the same vessel which contained water equal to three Mudds or thereabout. (Using translation from Muslim 321b)"
"1203","Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah (may peace he upon him) took a bath with five Makkuks of water and performed ablution with one Makkuk. Ibn Muthanna has used the words five Makakiyya, and Ibn Mu'adh narrated it from 'Abdullah b. 'Abdullah and he made no mention of Ibn Jabr. (Using translation from Muslim 325a)"
"1204","""I heard Anas bin Malik say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Wudu' with a Makkuk (cup) and Ghusl with five Makkuks (cups).'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 73)"
"1205","The Prophet ﷺ said: Angels do not enter the house where there is a picture, or a dog, or a person who is sexually defiled. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 227)"
"1206","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went around all his wives and only performed Ghusl once. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 263)"
"1207","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would visit all his wives in a single night, then he would perform ghusl (ritual bath) only once."
"1208","I asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): Did the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) have that much strength? So Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: We used to talk among ourselves that he was given the strength of thirty (30) men."
"1209","The Prophet ﷺ used to visit all his wives in one night and he had nine wives at that time. (Using translation from Bukhārī 284)"
"1210","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'If anyone of you has intercourse with his wife, then he wants to do it again, let him perform ablution.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 587)"
"1211","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When a man has intercourse with his wife and then wishes to do it again, he should perform ablution first. In this way, there will be more pleasure in doing it again."" Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: In narrating these last words, the narrator named Muslim bin Ibrahim is unique."
"1212","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: (Sometimes) I be"
"1213","Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that someti"
"1214","narrates: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he becomes in a state of janabah during the night, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed him to perform wudu, wash his private parts, and then go to sleep."
"1215","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, when he performs ablution (wudu), (then he can sleep)."
"1216","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Yes, if he wishes, he may perform wudu (ablution) and then (sleep)."
"1217","""If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to sleep while he was Junub, he would perform Wudu' as for prayer before sleeping."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 258)"
"1218","It was narrated from 'Aishah that if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to sleep while he was Junub, he would perform Wudu', and if he wanted to eat he would wash his hands. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 256)"
"1219","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Every Muslim man has to perform Ghusl one day in every seven, and that is on Friday.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1378)"
"1220","The reason for this is that experiencing a wet dream is a sign of adulthood, so it means that when a child becomes an adult or reaches the age of fifteen years, he will be considered an adult, even if he has not experienced a wet dream. According to him, Allah Almighty's statement is: ""And when your children reach puberty, let them seek permission as those before them sought permission."" So in this verse, Allah Almighty has commanded seeking permission for the one who becomes an adult, because here the word ""hulm"" means adulthood, and sometimes a child becomes an adult without experiencing a wet dream and becomes addressed by the command to seek permission just as he is addressed by this command when accompanied by a wet dream.)"
"1221","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the natural practices of Islam are taking a bath on Friday, using the miswak, keeping the moustache short, and letting the beard grow, because the Magians grow their moustaches and trim their beards, so you should oppose them; keep your moustaches short and let your beards grow."
"1222","The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""He remains pure until the next Friday,"" means that he remains pure from sins, because whoever participates in the Friday prayer with its conditions, the sins committed between this Friday and the next Friday are forgiven."
"1223","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) stating that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you come for Jumu'ah, perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"1224","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever comes for Jumu'ah should perform ghusl."
"1225","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever comes for Jumu'ah should perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"1226","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among men and women comes for Jumu'ah should perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"1227","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Taking a bath on Friday is obligatory upon every adult person and upon every adult woman among the women."
"1228","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Ghusl (taking a bath) on Friday is compulsory for every Muslim reaching the age of puberty."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 858)"
"1229","Taking bath on Friday is necessary for every adult. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 341)"
"1230","What is this hour (for attending the prayer)? He said: I was busy today and I did not return to my house when I heard the call (to Friday prayer), and I did no more but performed ablution only. Upon this Umar said: just ablution! You know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded (us) to take a bath (on Friday). (Using translation from Muslim 845a)"
"1231","If anyone performs ablution, doing it well, then come to the Friday prayer, listens and keeps silence, his sins between that time and the next Friday will be forgiven, with three days extra; but he who touches pebbles has caused an interruption. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1050)"
"1232","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""It is Allah's right upon every Muslim that he should perform ghusl (ritual bath) once a week, and if he has perfume, he should also apply it."",""The Prophet ﷺ  said"",""""""Indeed"","" Allah has a right upon every Muslim to perform Ghusl (ritual ablution) every seven days"","" on a specific day"","" and if he has perfume"","" he should apply it."""""""""
"1233","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Ghusl should be performed on Friday by everyone who has reached the age of puberty, and using the siwak, and he should put on whatever he is able of using perfume."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1383)"
"1234","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""It is obligatory upon every Muslim to perform ghusl once a week, and if he has it available, he should apply perfume."
"1235","I remember this about myself that we used to be with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and if it rained upon us, you would sense the smell of wet camels coming from among us."
"1236","The people (mostly) were workers and they would come for Friday prayer in the same condition, so it was said to them: If only you were to perform Ghusl. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 352)"
"1237","The people came for Jumu'a prayer from their houses in the neighbouring villages dressed in woollen garments on which dust was settled and this emitted a foul smell. A person among them (those who were dressed so) came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in my house. The Messenger of Allah (may peace he upon him) said to him: Were you to cleanse yourselves on this day. (Using translation from Muslim 847a)"
